# ERP Frontend

Follow [docs/ERP_FRONTEND_STANDARDS.md](../../docs/ERP_FRONTEND_STANDARDS.md).

- Preserve behavior; refactor incrementally. Do not remove features unless replaced.
- Workspace UI is ERP-dense: tables first, sticky toolbars/headers, right-side summaries, dialogs only for focused tasks.
- Use `ErpPageShell` for page chrome and `DataTable` (`variant="erp"`) for list pages.
- Support sort, filter, sticky header, column chooser, and row actions before inventing a new table.
- Posted documents (`COMPLETED`, `CANCELLED`, `VOIDED`, `CHECKED_OUT`) are read-only. Void/cancel instead of delete for money records.
- Show audit fields (`created_by`, timestamps, status) on document views via `AuditMeta`.
- ERP terms: Customers, Vendors, Journal Entries, Sales Invoices, Cost Centers. Keep Bookings/Stays where users expect them.
- Do not duplicate tax/overtime math in the UI; use tenant rates from the API (`utils/erp.js`).
- Keyboard: Escape closes dialogs; row click opens the record. Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`.
- Change only the files required for the page being refactored.
